{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3260","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3260","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3260\",\"parent_revision\":\"1db0de8807cf12b85bc4b4557500e110337696282247f6200dfa4db8659a9107\",\"root_revision\":\"1db0de8807cf12b85bc4b4557500e110337696282247f6200dfa4db8659a9107\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Refactor\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: 2026-08-28\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe SAM plan CLI (plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/sam_plan.py) exposes `--address` and `--plan-address` flags on the read/state/ready/status/update commands, and the work-backlog-item skill's documentation (references/workflows/resume/start.md, close/start.md, groom/groom-drift.md, work/sam-definition.md, work/post-planning.md, work/locate.md, work/start.md) consistently uses the variable name `plan_address` for the same value \u2014 including in places holding only a bare plan reference with no task component.\\n\\nObserved: a plan reference is an ID string identifying where a plan's data lives in the configured backend. The complete, canonical unique identifier is `P{hash}-{slug}` (e.g. `Pe9f0a1b2-backlog-lifecycle-process-gaps` \u2014 see `plan_id_from_path` in `sam_schema/core/backends/local_yaml.py`, which extracts the hash portion from a `P{id}-{slug}.yaml` filename); `addressing.py`'s resolver also accepts the bare hash/sequence prefix alone and resolves it via glob match against `P{id}-{slug}.*`. Plans are not files \u2014 the configured backend can be a YAML directory, SQLite, GitHub single-branch storage, or Beads \u2014 and this identifier has no filesystem or network-location semantics of its own regardless of backend.\\n\\n**Hypothesis**: `docs/TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md:157-158` draws an explicit id/address distinction (`P{id}` = \\\"plan logical identifier\\\" vs. `P{id}/T{M}` = \\\"task logical address\\\"), which would support \\\"address\\\" being intentionally reserved for the compound plan:task locator. This is only a hypothesis, not confirmed design intent \u2014 per the user, TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md predates the migration to the current backend-agnostic task protocol and describes the earlier file-bound task system; its filename-shaped examples (`~/.dh/projects/{slug}/plan/P{id}-{slug}.yaml`) and its own header (\\\"last synced 2026-08-12\\\", drift warning pointing to `sam_schema/core/models.py` as the real authority) suggest it may itself be stale and should not be relied on as evidence of current naming intent without separately verifying against `models.py`/the live backend implementations.\\n\\nImpact: regardless of that doc's reliability, `plan_address` reads as though a plan has a literal location, which is misleading given plans are backend-agnostic ID references, not files \u2014 this is independently true without relying on TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: work-backlog-item skill tightening pass, 2026-08-28\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-28\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"d7567f7e39fd51d016191aa7dc52ca5f6b2f3ca373d052e8b1dcb9cc99dd6545\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABRL5gjQ\"}"}